<title>UK: LIFFE white sugar lower at close.</title>
<headline>LIFFE white sugar lower at close.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>White sugar futures edged lower during the  late afternoon and October dropped to $326.00 a tonne before last  business at $327.00, down $1 from Thursday.</p>
<p>Turnover totalled 1,845 lots.</p>
<p>Traders said little fresh buying interest had emerged to prompt a  test of resistance around $330 a tonne and prices had fallen back  slightly from early highs under light liquidation orders.</p>
<p>In Paris October closed $1.30 down and turnover totalled 196 lots.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
